    <!-- Experimental: Android host bind (R1 / on-device build support) -->
    <string name="settings_section_experimental">Experimental / developer</string>
    <string name="settings_android_host_bind_toggle">Android host bind (/system, /apex)</string>
    <string name="settings_android_host_bind_toggle_desc">When ON, bind Android\'s /system and /apex inside PRoot/chroot so aarch64 ELFs (e.g. aapt2) can run. Takes effect on the next restart.</string>
    <string name="settings_android_host_bind_warning">⚠ This makes Android system directories visible inside the terminal. Understand the security implications before enabling.</string>
    <string name="settings_kitty_external_file_toggle">Kitty graphics: external file transfer</string>
    <string name="settings_kitty_external_file_toggle_desc">When ON, allow Kitty graphics t=f/t=t/t=s payloads to read files inside the active rootfs. OFF (default) discards all such requests. Required for some image viewer TUIs that send a path instead of base64.</string>
    <string name="settings_kitty_external_file_warning">⚠ Lets TUIs trigger reads of any file under the active distro rootfs. Off by default — only enable for trusted sessions.</string>
    <string name="settings_sgr_mouse_input_toggle">SGR mouse output (convert touch to mouse events)</string>
    <string name="settings_sgr_mouse_input_toggle_desc">When ON, taps are translated to TUI mouse events (SGR `?1006`). Required for some TUIs (calendar, file managers, multi-pane focus switching). Single tap = left click, long press = right click, one-finger drag = mouse motion. When OFF (default), taps are used by Z2Term itself (focus / text selection / scrolling). Two-finger swipe → wheel works the same regardless of this toggle.</string>
    <string name="settings_sgr_mouse_input_warning">⚠ When enabled, one-finger text selection and long-press menus are routed to the TUI. On screens that do not enable mouse capture (e.g. bash, less) taps still drive Z2Term as before.</string>
    <string name="settings_gui_clean_install_desc">Turn ON and open the GUI tab to reinstall the GUI-display packages (cache and all) — recovery for stuck DL/extraction. The check clears automatically on launch.</string>
    <string name="settings_gui_terminal_note">🖥 The terminal to open inside the GUI tab. If not installed yet it is auto-installed on first GUI start (Konsole, in KDE, has a large initial download — Wi-Fi recommended).</string>

